## Setup
Let $t_{1/2} \equiv 5730\,\mathrm{yr}$ be the half-life of carbon-14.

$$ \lambda := \frac{\ln 2}{t_{1/2}} \approx ? $$

$$ \frac{dN}{dt} = -\lambda N, \quad N(0) = N_0 $$

## Results
Fraction left after $10\,000$ years:
$$ \frac{N(10\,000\,\mathrm{yr})}{N_0} \approx ? $$

Age of a sample with 40 percent left:
$$ \operatorname{solve}_t \Big(\frac{N(t)}{N_0} = 0.40\Big) \approx ? $$

Figure: $N(t)/N_0$, $t \in [0, 30\,000\,\mathrm{yr}]$, with the half-lives marked.
